Thanks for your patience @plfort, and sorry it took so long to answer your question from July 2024. The feature is wanted, all seven review threads are resolved, so @artyuum's change request is stale.

I rebased on 8.2, squashed the eleven commits into one and pushed. Two things needed fixing, both from the branch having aged rather than from the original work.

**The `is_array()` guard had to be widened, not removed.** The branch dropped it:

```php
-if ($fields && !(\is_array($element) && $element = $this->reduceElementKeys($fields, $element))) {
+if ($fields && !$element = $this->reduceElementKeys($fields, $element)) {
```

That guard came from fced6c7bb77, which fixed a `TypeError` for non-array items such as `''`, `1` and `null` when `fields` is set. Removing it brings that back, and the branch also carried an older copy of the test file that no longer had `getValidCollectionValues`, the regression test for exactly that case, so CI could not have caught it. It is now:

```php
if ($fields && !((\is_array($element) || \is_object($element)) && $element = $this->reduceElementKeys($fields, $element))) {
```

**`getPropertyAccessor()` returned the concrete class.** The constructor accepts `PropertyAccessorInterface`, so injecting any decorator that implements the interface without extending `PropertyAccessor` threw:

> TypeError: UniqueValidator::getPropertyAccessor(): Return value must be of type PropertyAccessor, PropertyAccessorInterface@anonymous returned

It returns the interface now, matching `AbstractComparisonValidator`.

The test file had moved to `#[DataProvider]` attributes and the `validate()` helper of `ConstraintValidatorTestCase`, so I ported your cases onto the current file rather than restoring the old one. Your coverage is all there: public field, private field with a getter, property path, and mixed objects and arrays, on both the valid and the invalid provider.

Validator is green at 5294 tests, and reverting `UniqueValidator.php` fails 5 of the new cases.
